<title>HONG KONG: Indosuez W.I. Carr sets HK banks basket warrants.</title>
<headline>Indosuez W.I. Carr sets HK banks basket warrants.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indosuez W.I. Carr (Derivatives) Ltd said on Wednesday it is selling 1.30 billion American-style call warrants on shares of five Hong Kong banks.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises:</p>
<p> Bank of East Asia Ltd		    0.0321 shares</p>
<p> HSBC Holdings Plc			  0.0122 shares</p>
<p> Dao Heng Bank Group Ltd		  0.0115 shares</p>
<p> Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd	0.0211 shares</p>
<p> Union Bank of Hong Kong Ltd	    0.0219 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one share.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	 HK$4.3694	PREMIUM	 9.5 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	  HK$0.0947	GEARING	 5.2x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	   15.JAN.98	EXER LOT	10,000</p>
<p> LISTING		HONG KONG</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT     HK$4.8549</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
